  "text": "Allergies:\ncodeine / naproxen\n\nChief Complaint:\nL breast cancer\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMs. ___ is a ___ year old female who presents with a recently\ndiagnosed left breast cancer.  The patient is being cared for by\nDr. ___ our ___ team and is noted to have nodal\ninvolvement and an axillary sampling/dissection has been\nrecommended.  The patient is being evaluated by PRS for\nconsideration of a prophylactic lymphovenous bypass as a\nlymphedema risk reducing procedure (LYMPHA).  The patient states\nthat current discussions for therapy have included possible\nchemotherapy and radiation therapy.  Of note, the patient is\nscheduled to undergo simultaneous bilateral TE placements by Dr.\n___.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nMs ___ was taken to the OR with Drs ___, and ___ \non ___ - please see separately dictated operative notes for \ndetails.  Post operatively she recovered in the pacu and later \nthe surgical floor without event.  on POD1, her incisions were \nclean dry and intact, drains were serosanguinous, she was \nvoiding independently, and tolerating a regular diet.  However, \nher pain was poorly controlled and she did not feel comfortable \ngoing home.  She was transitioned from a PCA to oral pain \nmedicine in an effort to achieve longer lasting pain control. \nShe found oxycodone inadequate so she was switched to dilaudid.  \nDiazepam was added for muscle spasm.  IV Tylenol seemed to help \nher pain the most.  By POD2 she was transitioned to standing PO \nTylenol, 5 mg diazepam, and 4mg dilaudid.  She still felt pain \ncontrol was suboptimal, stating that she was expecting to not \nhave pain post op, but rather \"tightness.\" Expectations for \nnormal post operative recovery were reviewed.  Pt expressed her \ninterest in going home.  Later that day she reported inadequate \npain control.  We offered to increase dilaudid to 6mg but would \nneed to observe her for four hours on the new dose.  She refused \nthis change and requested to go home instead.  All vital signs \nwere stable, exam was unchanged, and she was able to complete \nADLs.  She was discharged to home in a stable condition.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nL breast cancer",
